meta {
  name: Reset Abnormal Flag Logic to Bold (SiteAdmin)
  type: http
  seq: 14
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/siteadmin/master-data/abnormal-flag-logic/reset-to-bold?tenantId={{tenantId}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  tenantId: {{tenantId}}
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{siteAdminToken}}
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
  test("returns an update summary", function () {
    const d = res.getBody().data;
    expect(d).to.have.property("referenceRangesUpdated");
    expect(d).to.have.property("referenceValuesUpdated");
  });
}

docs {
  **SiteAdmin maintenance** — for the tenant given by the `tenantId` **query
  param**, normalise the "Abnormal Flag Logic" of all its existing reference
  ranges **and** reference values from **Bold and Red** (`BOLD_AND_RED`) to
  **Bold** (`BOLD_ONLY`). Any row carrying a different flag (`ITALIC`, …) is left
  untouched, and no other reference-value setting is changed.

  Auth: **SiteAdmin** token (`jwt-siteadmin`), requires `master-data:write`
  (CONTENT_ADMIN and above). `@Public()` only opts out of the *business* JWT guard.

  ## Query params

  | Param      | Type | Required | Notes                                             |
  | ---------- | ---- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------- |
  | `tenantId` | UUID | **yes**  | The tenant whose test records are updated. Accepted here on purpose — SiteAdmin cross-tenant tooling (CLAUDE.md §4.7). |

  ## Response (`data`)

  ```json
  {
    "referenceRangesUpdated": 128,
    "referenceValuesUpdated": 42
  }
  ```

  ## Notes & errors

  - Runs inside an RLS tenant transaction, so it works whether or not
    `RLS_ENABLED` is set. SITE_ADMIN template rows (`tenantId IS NULL`) are
    platform content, not a tenant's master data, and are **out of scope**.
  - Soft-deleted rows (`deletedAt`) are skipped.
  - Idempotent: re-running after it has run updates 0 rows (nothing is
    `BOLD_AND_RED` anymore).
  - `400 VALIDATION_ERROR` if `tenantId` is missing or not a UUID.
  - `404 TENANT_NOT_FOUND` if `tenantId` does not exist.
}
